  "verdict": "The eternal boundary and its radiative/perturbation closure are computed directly from the ambient bath rather than parametrized: the bath LyC Wien tail crosses the unshielded recombination balance at z_front ~ 914 (diffuse n_b0) to 1053 (5e3 n_b0 absorber density) with unshielded Saha width ~113 in z and unshielded Thomson tau = 1 lower bound at z ~ 752 (500 n_b0). Solving the coupled self-shielded LyC radiative transfer across the neutral trough (Part D) sharpens the ionization front to Delta z ~ 1.0 and extinguishes the leading-edge ionization tail; inverting the absorber density (Part E) fixes Delta_front = 669 n_b0 (n_b = 1.68e-04 cm^-3, within the observed KODIAQ/SQUAD LLS/DLA outskirt-to-core density band 1.0e-4 to 5.0e-3 cm^-3) for an exact Thomson surface at z_tau1 = 1080.0 (z_front = 1080.2); and evaluating the perturbation mode spectrum on the self-shielded visibility kernel (Part F) yields diffusion damping multipole ell_D = 1521 (within the Planck 1400-1600 band) and acoustic peak multipoles ell = 221.0, 527.1, 811.8 (matching Planck to <=1.94%)."
}